<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine weekly official crop progress.</title>
<headline>Argentine weekly official crop progress.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine farmers had harvested 9,300 hectares of 1996/97 wheat by Oct 25, the Agriculture Secretariat said Thursday in its weekly report.</p>
<p>Recent frosts in Argentina's southern wheat belt caused little damage to the wheat crop, it said. It estimated that this season's wheat output will be 14.9 million tonnes, up from 9.2 million tonnes in 1995/96. Maize sowing, which reached 45.4 percent of total intentions, was paralyzed in Chaco, Salta and Santiago del Estero. Sunflower sowing reached 27.2 percent of intentions. Cotton sowing reached 9.6 percent of an intended 969,000 hectares.  </p>
<p>Intended total planting (thousands of hectares) and the percentage already sown (year-earlier in brackets). Harvest levels (thousands of hectares) and as a percentage of planted area, (year-earlier in brackets). Yield in quintals per hectare.</p>
<p> ..........Planting.............Harvest..................Yield</p>
<p> Wheat     6,866  100.0(100.0)     9.3    0.1   (0.0)   (16.6)</p>
<p> Maize     3,796   45.4 (53.9)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Soybeans    n/a    n/a  (n/a)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Sunflower 2,999   27.2 (36.5)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Sorghum     782    3.4  (4.3)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Cotton	969    9.6  (n/a)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p>-- Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541-318-0655</p>
